---
// Private, unlisted cover letter. noindex + excluded from the sitemap (see
// astro.config.mjs) + not linked anywhere on the site. Shareable by link only.
import Base from '../../layouts/Base.astro';
---

<Base
  title="Pablo Corzo — Principal Product Manager, Engagement Journeys"
  description="Cover letter — Pablo Corzo for Spotify."
  theme="light"
  noindex={true}
>
  <article class="shell pt-[46px] pb-24">
    <header class="border-b-2 border-foreground pb-6">
      <p class="t-label text-accent-text">Cover letter</p>
      <h1 class="t-title font-edo mt-3 max-w-[20ch]">Pablo Corzo</h1>
    </header>

    <div class="mx-[15px] mt-10 max-w-[75%]">
      <p class="t-label text-dim">Re: Principal Product Manager, Engagement Journeys</p>

      <div class="letter font-ui mt-9">
        <p>Spotify Hiring Team,</p>

        <p>
          Like millions of people, Spotify is part of the daily rhythm of my life. What keeps me
          fascinated by what you build goes beyond the music itself. It is the quiet 'magic' of how
          experimentation and personalization transform a massive catalog into something deeply
          personal and nostalgic. The 'Made for' and 'Release Radar' features alone have enhanced my
          experience tremendously, and the 'Prompted Playlist' beta feature has me rediscovering
          songs I had forgotten about constantly.
        </p>

        <p>
          Over the past decade, my work has centered on building consumer and data products where
          discovery, behavior, and experimentation intersect. Whether leading experimentation and
          partnering with personalization at Best Buy or steering data, media, and
          <a href="/writing/experimentation-platforms-are-becoming-organizational-memory"
            >experimentation platforms</a
          > at Monks, my focus has always been on true user value. I care deeply about the intricate
          balance between quantitative rigor (through measurement frameworks that shy away from
          <a href="/writing/learning-is-the-product">vanity metrics</a>), and crafting experiences
          that feel intuitive and authentic.
        </p>

        <p>
          What draws me specifically to the Principal Product Manager role in the Surfaces Studio is
          the chance to shape engagement journeys across multiple formats and touch-points for a
          product and brand I already admire. As we step into an era where
          <a href="/ideas/ai-foundations-for-product-leaders">AI and agent technologies</a> can make
          discovery feel even more natural, the challenge is about building genuine trust
          and long-term relationships with listeners without making it feel like an invasion or
          overstep. It means looking at how someone transitions from a casual listener to someone
          deeply connected to music, podcasts, or audiobooks, and making that path and engagement
          feel seamless.
        </p>

        <p>
          I am a hands-on builder who loves exploring how new tech can solve real human problems. I
          am also really interested in understanding how to do so without degrading our ways of
          behaving, thinking and connecting. I am energized by the thought of collaborating with the
          teams behind features like the ones I mentioned above and many others to create meaningful
          impact. I would be thrilled to be considered for this role, as it would be the opportunity
          of a lifetime.
        </p>

        <p class="signoff">
          Thank you,<br />
          <span class="font-edo text-[1.35rem]">Pablo Corzo</span>
        </p>
      </div>
    </div>
  </article>
</Base>

<style>
  .letter p {
    font-size: 1.0625rem;
    line-height: 1.72;
    color: var(--body);
    margin-top: 1.35rem;
  }
  .letter p:first-child {
    margin-top: 0;
  }
  .letter a {
    color: var(--accent-text);
    text-decoration: underline;
    text-decoration-thickness: 1px;
    text-underline-offset: 2px;
    text-decoration-color: color-mix(in srgb, var(--accent-text) 38%, transparent);
    transition: text-decoration-color 0.15s ease;
  }
  .letter a:hover {
    text-decoration-color: var(--accent-text);
  }
  .letter .signoff {
    margin-top: 2.25rem;
    line-height: 1.5;
  }
</style>
